    "body": "## Summary\n- expire stale `PAYMENT_REQUIRED` job publications synchronously when the owner reads them\n- release reserved wallet funds through the existing idempotent `JOB_PUBLICATION_RELEASE` ledger operation\n- keep Stripe PaymentIntent creation rollback-safe: expired payment attempts are still rejected without trying to persist a release in the same exception-rolling-back transaction\n- keep the scheduled expiry worker as a background cleanup path while making owner-facing status refresh deterministic\n- add focused regression coverage for expired vs still-active reservations\n\n## Correctness / security\n- ownership is checked before lazy expiry\n- publication rows are locked before the state transition\n- wallet release remains idempotently keyed by publication id, preventing double-credit across scheduler/access races\n- no payment credentials or private job payloads are exposed\n- the Stripe expiry rejection remains unchanged and cannot accidentally roll back a wallet-release mutation because that mutation is not performed on the throwing path\n\n## Validation\nRequired PR workflows must be green on the latest head before merge.",
